<title>UK: BIL sets $150 million 10-year subordinated FRN.</title>
<headline>BIL sets $150 million 10-year subordinated FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities and Banque Internationale a Luxembourg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE INTERNATIONALE A LUXEMBOURG SA</p>
<p> AMT	  $150 MLN BASE	  3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	 JUL.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +37.5 BP  PAY DATE    09.JUL.97</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  ISS PRICE  99.74     FULL FEES   0.50</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   REOFFER    99.74</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  LUX	 TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
